<EnglishDocLayout
  title="Context, Task, Boundaries, Verification"
  description="Freeze a vague request into a four-part contract an agent can execute and a reviewer can verify."
  chineseHref="/start-here/context-task-verification/"
>
  <h2>Why one-line requests fail</h2>
  <p>
    “Improve this page,” “fix login,” and “move the project to a new framework” express direction,
    not a decision boundary. The agent must guess the entry point, finish line, allowed changes,
    and verification method.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Cell</th><th>Question</th><th>Minimum evidence</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Context</td><td>What is true now, and where is the entry point?</td><td>Repository, branch, key files, reproduction, or baseline</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Task</td><td>Who can observe what change when this is done?</td><td>One visible or measurable outcome</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Boundaries</td><td>What may change, what is forbidden, and when must work stop?</td><td>Allowed paths, hard stops, and escalation rules</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Verification</td><td>What proves completion rather than plausibility?</td><td>Command, exit status, diff, page, or human checkpoint</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Make the outcome observable</h2>
  <p>
    Weak goal: “Improve onboarding.” Runnable goal: “A first-time reader can choose one of three
    task-based routes within two clicks; every target route exists after the static build; no
    external script is added.”
  </p>

  <h2>Set boundaries before execution</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>File boundary:</strong> allowed paths and user changes that must be preserved.</li>
    <li><strong>Action boundary:</strong> dependency installation, network access, deletion, commit, push, or deployment.</li>
    <li><strong>Escalation boundary:</strong> secrets, paid calls, production data, or ambiguous product choices.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Verify at three levels</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Deterministic:</strong> tests, lint, typecheck, link scan, or validator.</li>
    <li><strong>Change hygiene:</strong> <code>git diff --check</code>, changed-file list, and sensitive-data scan.</li>
    <li><strong>Human:</strong> browser walkthrough, visual review, copy, and risk judgment.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="a-copyable-template">A copyable template</h2>
  <pre><code># Goal
Who can observe what change when this is complete?

# Context
- Current state:
- Key entry point:
- Original evidence or error:

# Scope and boundaries
- Allowed files:
- Forbidden actions:
- Must request approval for:

# Verification
- Fastest relevant check:
- Full mechanical check:
- Human checkpoint:
- Evidence to retain on failure:

# Delivery
Changes, evidence, open risks, and next action.</code></pre>
</EnglishDocLayout>
